<div class="page-shell legal-page"><span class="eyebrow">Your source stays yours</span><h1>Privacy at CodeDiff</h1><p class="legal-lede">CodeDiff is designed to compare code and text without creating a history unless you choose to save one.</p><section><h2>Comparisons</h2><p>When you submit a comparison, the two text versions are sent to the application to enforce account limits and return the comparison workspace. Unsaved versions are not stored as comparison records or included in usage analytics. Comparison usage records contain the account identifier, time, and selected language, but not source text.</p></section><section><h2>Saved comparisons</h2><p>If you sign in and select “Save this comparison,” CodeDiff stores both versions in your private account history. Only you and authorized administrators can access saved comparisons. You can delete a saved comparison from your account.</p></section><section><h2>Accounts and requests</h2><p>CodeDiff stores account details needed for sign-in, email verification, password recovery, usage limits, and lifetime access requests. Administrative access grants and review decisions are recorded in an audit log.</p></section><section><h2>Uploaded files</h2><p>Text files are read as UTF-8 content and are never executed. Do not upload files you are not authorized to use. File comparison currently supports text and code only.</p></section><section><h2>Retention and contact</h2><p>You can remove saved comparison records from your account. Account and audit records may be retained as needed to operate and secure the service. For privacy questions, contact the CodeDiff service administrator.</p></section></div>
